  :adr/pattern-6493 "sealed Factoring-LLM advisor + independent Factoring Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on cloud-itonami-isic-6492's Store/Registry/Governor/Phase/Advisor/Operation/Sim shape and cloud-itonami-isic-6499's multi-actuation shape; registered directly at :implemented with no prior :spec placeholder for this ISIC at all"
  :adr/isic-citation "ISIC Rev.5 class 6493 = Factoring activities, division 649, a genuine standalone class distinct from 6491/6492/6494/6495/6499 -- verified against the official ISIC Rev.5 structure CSV and explanatory-notes PDF (UN Statistics Division). Full explanatory note: 'This class covers the activity of purchasing accounts receivable (i.e., invoices) from third parties at a discount. This class excludes: debt financing undertaken with account receivables as collateral, see 6495.'"
  :adr/zentoshin-motivation "全東信 (Zentoshin), a Japanese card-settlement/early-payment-advance company, filed for bankruptcy 2026-07 with JPY 115.1 billion in liabilities after ~20 years of alleged accounting fraud (決算粉飾) hid its true insolvency; ~200,000 merchants affected, ~JPY 5B+ stuck. Owner asked for a design structurally preventing this failure class via distributed funding, open source, and fair pricing as load-bearing implementation requirements, not disclaimers."
  :adr/two-actuation-6493 "two actuation events (:actuation/advance-cash, :actuation/release-reserve), both permanently excluded from every phase's :auto set, matching cloud-itonami-isic-6499's multi-actuation shape rather than every single-actuation sibling's one member; collection is deliberately NOT an actuation (inbound receipt, not an act the factor originates)"
  :adr/underwriting-inversion-6493 "credit risk properly assessed against the ACCOUNT DEBTOR (a third party who never submits a proposal), not the client, unlike credit.governor's (6492) borrower-side affordability check; the LEGAL spec-basis by contrast still follows the CLIENT's jurisdiction, mirroring UCC Article 9's own choice-of-law rule -- a deliberate, non-symmetric split between legal domicile and credit-risk domicile"
  :adr/distinctive-check-6493 "aggregate-exposure is a pure fn whose ground truth is an AGGREGATION over MULTIPLE stored receivable records for one counterparty axis (debtor/funder/whole-book), verified distinct from both templates read directly for this build (credit.governor reads a single record's own fields; vcfund.governor recomputes from a proposal's claim, neither aggregates across multiple stored records); debtor-concentration-ceiling-exceeded-violations and funder-concentration-ceiling-exceeded-violations both reuse the EXISTING direct-comparison MAXIMUM-ceiling family, no new comparison family claimed, and no whole-fleet-first claimed (only verified against the two templates read directly)"
  :adr/anti-zentoshin-mitigations-6493 "three first-class, load-bearing HARD-check mitigations: (1) publicly-queryable ledger-recomputed solvency attestation (solvency-attestation-mismatch-violations + solvency-attestation-stale-or-missing-violations, never a self-reported number) (2) distributed non-custodial funding via named funders with recorded capacity (funder-concentration-ceiling-exceeded-violations, no single funder can back enough of the book to cascade) (3) fair non-discretionary pricing via a published versioned fee schedule (fee-rate-mismatch-violations, exact-match family)"
  :adr/registry-bookkeeping-6493 "kotoba-lang/industry: brand-new '6493' entry (no prior :spec placeholder existed at all), registered directly at :implemented. Fleet-wide maturity 146 -> 147 :implemented out of 647 total registry entries (up from 646, a new class-level row not a tier promotion). test/kotoba/industry_test.clj maturity-summary assertion + dedicated maturity test updated; docs/cloud-itonami.md's maturity-tier count line (drifted to a stale 106/36/504 split through many untracked promotion ADRs predating this build) refreshed to actual ground truth as part of this registration."
  :adr/west-pin-bookkeeping-6493 "manifest/west.yml's industry project pin advanced via GitHub API single-entry commit workflow (repos.edn :manifest-workflow, the only sanctioned path), verified with nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check from a properly west-topdir-isolated sibling worktree; advanced twice (once for the registration commit, once more for a small follow-up citation-accuracy fix)"
  :adr/sequence-ordinal-honesty-note "earlier post-batch ADRs (6612 through 6491) maintained an explicit hand-counted 'Nth vertical outside the original batch' sequence; that convention became impractical once the fleet passed ~40 verticals and started registering multi-ISIC batches in single ADRs (petroleum/heavy-industry) and, most recently, a CRM-family sibling-actor roadmap framing (5820/6201/6202) with no stated ordinal at all. This ADR reports the number computed DIRECTLY from the registry's own current ground truth instead of guessing or perpetuating a silently-abandoned counter: 146 :implemented entries prior to this build, minus the 8 ISICs in ADR-2607032000's original batch, is 138 verticals built outside that batch to date -- this build is the 139th by direct count"
  :adr/known-issue-6492-mislabeling "cloud-itonami-isic-6492's README claims 'ISIC Rev.5 6492: Other credit granting' but the OFFICIAL Rev.5 title for 6492 is 'International trade financing activities'; 6492's actual implemented content (loan intake/underwriting/disbursement, general lending) structurally matches official code 6495 'Other credit granting activities' instead. Pre-existing mislabeling, NOT fixed by this ADR (6492 is a read-only template for this build) -- recorded for a future ADR, no claim on 6495 made here"
